Valtz includes, unmodified, MOSS-Image's prompt-enhancer skill
(https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image, commit
20f5592077916ec8d439bed7b34d18e45c20d657):

  skills/moss-image-prompt-enhancer/SKILL.md
  skills/moss-image-prompt-enhancer/references/layout.md
  skills/moss-image-prompt-enhancer/scripts/compile_prompt.py

SKILL.md and references/layout.md are used, as the instructions their
makers publish, by Valtz's prompt enhancer when the target model is
MOSS-Image. compile_prompt.py is not run: Valtz compiles the drafts it
describes with code of its own that follows it (the core's
assist::moss_image_prompt), and keeps it here as that code's reference.
